WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.690
His main connection is viscosity to volcano shape. Viscosity means resistance

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:09.030
to flow. Watch how each eruption adds material to the slopes.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.989
Low-viscosity basalt spreads far, building a broad shield such as Hawaii.

00:00:14.989 --> 00:00:19.627
More viscous magma and successive eruption deposits build a steeper composite

00:00:19.627 --> 00:00:20.049
volcano.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.109
Mount Fuji and Mount Saint Helens were his composite examples. More

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.368
silica generally increases viscosity. Explain why the material spreads out or

00:00:29.368 --> 00:00:30.142
builds up.
